#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "gitprotocol-v2(5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:7
msgid "gitprotocol-v2 - Git Wire Protocol, Version 2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "<over-the-wire-protocol>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:18
msgid ""
"This document presents a specification for a version 2 of Git's wire "
"protocol.  Protocol v2 will improve upon v1 in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:21
msgid ""
"Instead of multiple service names, multiple commands will be supported by a "
"single service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:24
msgid ""
"Easily extendable as capabilities are moved into their own section of the "
"protocol, no longer being hidden behind a NUL byte and limited by the size "
"of a pkt-line"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:26
msgid ""
"Separate out other information hidden behind NUL bytes (e.g. agent string as "
"a capability and symrefs can be requested using 'ls-refs')"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:27
msgid "Reference advertisement will be omitted unless explicitly requested"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:28
msgid "ls-refs command to explicitly request some refs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:30
msgid ""
"Designed with http and stateless-rpc in mind.  With clear flush semantics "
"the http remote helper can simply act as a proxy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:36
msgid ""
"In protocol v2 communication is command oriented.  When first contacting a "
"server a list of capabilities will be advertised.  Some of these "
"capabilities will be commands which a client can request be executed.  Once "
"a command has completed, a client can reuse the connection and request that "
"other commands be executed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Packet-Line Framing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:42
msgid ""
"All communication is done using packet-line framing, just as in v1.  See "
"linkgit:gitprotocol-pack[5] and linkgit:gitprotocol-common[5] for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:44
msgid "In protocol v2 these special packets will have the following semantics:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:46
msgid "'0000' Flush Packet (flush-pkt) - indicates the end of a message"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:47
msgid "'0001' Delimiter Packet (delim-pkt) - separates sections of a message"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:49
msgid ""
"'0002' Response End Packet (response-end-pkt) - indicates the end of a "
"response for stateless connections"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initial Client Request"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:59
msgid ""
"In general a client can request to speak protocol v2 by sending `version=2` "
"through the respective side-channel for the transport being used which "
"inevitably sets `GIT_PROTOCOL`.  More information can be found in "
"linkgit:gitprotocol-pack[5] and linkgit:gitprotocol-http[5], as well as the "
"`GIT_PROTOCOL` definition in `git.txt`. In all cases the response from the "
"server is the capability advertisement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git Transport"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:65
msgid ""
"When using the git:// transport, you can request to use protocol v2 by "
"sending \"version=2\" as an extra parameter:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "   003egit-upload-pack /project.git\\0host=myserver.com\\0\\0version=2\\0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSH and File Transport"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:75
msgid ""
"When using either the ssh:// or file:// transport, the GIT_PROTOCOL "
"environment variable must be set explicitly to include \"version=2\".  The "
"server may need to be configured to allow this environment variable to pass."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP Transport"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:82
msgid ""
"When using the http:// or https:// transport a client makes a \"smart\" "
"info/refs request as described in linkgit:gitprotocol-http[5] and requests "
"that v2 be used by supplying \"version=2\" in the `Git-Protocol` header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   C: GET $GIT_URL/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack HTTP/1.0\n"
"   C: Git-Protocol: version=2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:87
msgid "A v2 server would reply:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   S: 200 OK\n"
"   S: <Some headers>\n"
"   S: ...\n"
"   S:\n"
"   S: 000eversion 2\\n\n"
"   S: <capability-advertisement>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:97
msgid ""
"Subsequent requests are then made directly to the service "
"`$GIT_URL/git-upload-pack`. (This works the same for git-receive-pack)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:100
msgid "Uses the `--http-backend-info-refs` option to linkgit:git-upload-pack[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:103
msgid ""
"The server may need to be configured to pass this header's contents via the "
"`GIT_PROTOCOL` variable. See the discussion in `git-http-backend.txt`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capability Advertisement"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:114
msgid ""
"A server which decides to communicate (based on a request from a client)  "
"using protocol version 2, notifies the client by sending a version string in "
"its initial response followed by an advertisement of its capabilities.  Each "
"capability is a key with an optional value.  Clients must ignore all unknown "
"keys.  Semantics of unknown values are left to the definition of each key.  "
"Some capabilities will describe commands which can be requested to be "
"executed by the client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    capability-advertisement = protocol-version\n"
"\t\t\t       capability-list\n"
"\t\t\t       flush-pkt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    protocol-version = PKT-LINE(\"version 2\" LF)\n"
"    capability-list = *capability\n"
"    capability = PKT-LINE(key[=value] LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    key = 1*(ALPHA | DIGIT | \"-_\")\n"
"    value = 1*(ALPHA | DIGIT | \" -_.,?\\/{}[]()<>!@#$%^&*+=:;\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Request"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:134
msgid ""
"After receiving the capability advertisement, a client can then issue a "
"request to select the command it wants with any particular capabilities or "
"arguments.  There is then an optional section where the client can provide "
"any command specific parameters or queries.  Only a single command can be "
"requested at a time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    request = empty-request | command-request\n"
"    empty-request = flush-pkt\n"
"    command-request = command\n"
"\t\t      capability-list\n"
"\t\t      delim-pkt\n"
"\t\t      command-args\n"
"\t\t      flush-pkt\n"
"    command = PKT-LINE(\"command=\" key LF)\n"
"    command-args = *command-specific-arg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    command-specific-args are packet line framed arguments defined by\n"
"    each individual command.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:155
msgid ""
"The server will then check to ensure that the client's request is comprised "
"of a valid command as well as valid capabilities which were advertised.  If "
"the request is valid the server will then execute the command.  A server "
"MUST wait till it has received the client's entire request before issuing a "
"response.  The format of the response is determined by the command being "
"executed, but in all cases a flush-pkt indicates the end of the response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:161
msgid ""
"When a command has finished, and the client has received the entire response "
"from the server, a client can either request that another command be "
"executed or can terminate the connection.  A client may optionally send an "
"empty request consisting of just a flush-pkt to indicate that no more "
"requests will be made."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:169
msgid ""
"There are two different types of capabilities: normal capabilities, which "
"can be used to convey information or alter the behavior of a request, and "
"commands, which are the core actions that a client wants to perform (fetch, "
"push, etc)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:177
msgid ""
"Protocol version 2 is stateless by default.  This means that all commands "
"must only last a single round and be stateless from the perspective of the "
"server side, unless the client has requested a capability indicating that "
"state should be maintained by the server.  Clients MUST NOT require state "
"management on the server side in order to function correctly.  This permits "
"simple round-robin load-balancing on the server side, without needing to "
"worry about state management."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "agent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:192
msgid ""
"The server can advertise the `agent` capability with a value `X` (in the "
"form `agent=X`) to notify the client that the server is running version "
"`X`.  The client may optionally send its own agent string by including the "
"`agent` capability with a value `Y` (in the form `agent=Y`) in its request "
"to the server (but it MUST NOT do so if the server did not advertise the "
"agent capability). The `X` and `Y` strings may contain any printable ASCII "
"characters except space (i.e., the byte range 32 < x < 127), and are "
"typically of the form \"package/version\" (e.g., \"git/1.8.3.1\"). The agent "
"strings are purely informative for statistics and debugging purposes, and "
"MUST NOT be used to programmatically assume the presence or absence of "
"particular features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "ls-refs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:199
msgid ""
"`ls-refs` is the command used to request a reference advertisement in v2.  "
"Unlike the current reference advertisement, ls-refs takes in arguments which "
"can be used to limit the refs sent from the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:203
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:251
msgid ""
"Additional features not supported in the base command will be advertised as "
"the value of the command in the capability advertisement in the form of a "
"space separated list of features: \"<command>=<feature-1> <feature-2>\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:205
msgid "ls-refs takes in the following arguments:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "symrefs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:209
msgid ""
"In addition to the object pointed by it, show the underlying ref pointed by "
"it when showing a symbolic ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "peel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:212
msgid "Show peeled tags."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:213
#, no-wrap
msgid "ref-prefix <prefix>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:220
msgid ""
"When specified, only references having a prefix matching one of the provided "
"prefixes are displayed. Multiple instances may be given, in which case "
"references matching any prefix will be shown. Note that this is purely for "
"optimization; a server MAY show refs not matching the prefix if it chooses, "
"and clients should filter the result themselves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:223
msgid ""
"If the 'unborn' feature is advertised the following argument can be included "
"in the client's request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:224
#, no-wrap
msgid "unborn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:228
msgid ""
"The server will send information about HEAD even if it is a symref pointing "
"to an unborn branch in the form \"unborn HEAD symref-target:<target>\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:230
msgid "The output of ls-refs is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:238
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    output = *ref\n"
"\t     flush-pkt\n"
"    obj-id-or-unborn = (obj-id | \"unborn\")\n"
"    ref = PKT-LINE(obj-id-or-unborn SP refname *(SP ref-attribute) LF)\n"
"    ref-attribute = (symref | peeled)\n"
"    symref = \"symref-target:\" symref-target\n"
"    peeled = \"peeled:\" obj-id\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:240
#, no-wrap
msgid "fetch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:247
msgid ""
"`fetch` is the command used to fetch a packfile in v2.  It can be looked at "
"as a modified version of the v1 fetch where the ref-advertisement is "
"stripped out (since the `ls-refs` command fills that role) and the message "
"format is tweaked to eliminate redundancies and permit easy addition of "
"future extensions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:253
msgid "A `fetch` request can take the following arguments:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:254
#, no-wrap
msgid "want <oid>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:258
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server an object which the client wants to retrieve.  Wants "
"can be anything and are not limited to advertised objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:259
#, no-wrap
msgid "have <oid>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:264
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server an object which the client has locally.  This allows "
"the server to make a packfile which only contains the objects that the "
"client needs. Multiple 'have' lines can be supplied."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "done"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:270
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server that negotiation should terminate (or not even begin "
"if performing a clone) and that the server should use the information "
"supplied in the request to construct the packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "thin-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:278
msgid ""
"Request that a thin pack be sent, which is a pack with deltas which "
"reference base objects not contained within the pack (but are known to exist "
"at the receiving end). This can reduce the network traffic significantly, "
"but it requires the receiving end to know how to \"thicken\" these packs by "
"adding the missing bases to the pack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "no-progress"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:284
msgid ""
"Request that progress information that would normally be sent on side-band "
"channel 2, during the packfile transfer, should not be sent.  However, the "
"side-band channel 3 is still used for error responses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "include-tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:288
msgid ""
"Request that annotated tags should be sent if the objects they point to are "
"being sent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:289
#, no-wrap
msgid "ofs-delta"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:293
msgid ""
"Indicate that the client understands PACKv2 with delta referring to its base "
"by position in pack rather than by an oid.  That is, they can read "
"OBJ_OFS_DELTA (aka type 6) in a packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:297
msgid ""
"If the 'shallow' feature is advertised the following arguments can be "
"included in the clients request as well as the potential addition of the "
"'shallow-info' section in the server's response as explained below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:298
#, no-wrap
msgid "shallow <oid>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:305
msgid ""
"A client must notify the server of all commits for which it only has shallow "
"copies (meaning that it doesn't have the parents of a commit) by supplying a "
"'shallow <oid>' line for each such object so that the server is aware of the "
"limitations of the client's history.  This is so that the server is aware "
"that the client may not have all objects reachable from such commits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "deepen <depth>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:309
msgid ""
"Requests that the fetch/clone should be shallow having a commit depth of "
"<depth> relative to the remote side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:310
#, no-wrap
msgid "deepen-relative"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:315
msgid ""
"Requests that the semantics of the \"deepen\" command be changed to indicate "
"that the depth requested is relative to the client's current shallow "
"boundary, instead of relative to the requested commits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:316
#, no-wrap
msgid "deepen-since <timestamp>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:321
msgid ""
"Requests that the shallow clone/fetch should be cut at a specific time, "
"instead of depth.  Internally it's equivalent to doing \"git rev-list "
"--max-age=<timestamp>\". Cannot be used with \"deepen\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "deepen-not <rev>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:328
msgid ""
"Requests that the shallow clone/fetch should be cut at a specific revision "
"specified by '<rev>', instead of a depth.  Internally it's equivalent of "
"doing \"git rev-list --not <rev>\".  Cannot be used with \"deepen\", but can "
"be used with \"deepen-since\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:331
msgid ""
"If the 'filter' feature is advertised, the following argument can be "
"included in the client's request:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:332
#, no-wrap
msgid "filter <filter-spec>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:343
msgid ""
"Request that various objects from the packfile be omitted using one of "
"several filtering techniques. These are intended for use with partial clone "
"and partial fetch operations. See `rev-list` for possible \"filter-spec\" "
"values. When communicating with other processes, senders SHOULD translate "
"scaled integers (e.g. \"1k\") into a fully-expanded form (e.g. \"1024\") to "
"aid interoperability with older receivers that may not understand "
"newly-invented scaling suffixes. However, receivers SHOULD accept the "
"following suffixes: 'k', 'm', and 'g' for 1024, 1048576, and 1073741824, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:347
msgid ""
"If the 'ref-in-want' feature is advertised, the following argument can be "
"included in the client's request as well as the potential addition of the "
"'wanted-refs' section in the server's response as explained below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:348
#, no-wrap
msgid "want-ref <ref>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:353
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server that the client wants to retrieve a particular ref, "
"where <ref> is the full name of a ref on the server.  It is a protocol error "
"to send want-ref for the same ref more than once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:356
msgid ""
"If the 'sideband-all' feature is advertised, the following argument can be "
"included in the client's request:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:357
#, no-wrap
msgid "sideband-all"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:363
msgid ""
"Instruct the server to send the whole response multiplexed, not just the "
"packfile section. All non-flush and non-delim PKT-LINE in the response (not "
"only in the packfile section) will then start with a byte indicating its "
"sideband (1, 2, or 3), and the server may send \"0005\\2\" (a PKT-LINE of "
"sideband 2 with no payload) as a keepalive packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:369
msgid ""
"If the 'packfile-uris' feature is advertised, the following argument can be "
"included in the client's request as well as the potential addition of the "
"'packfile-uris' section in the server's response as explained below. Note "
"that at most one `packfile-uris` line can be sent to the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:370
#, no-wrap
msgid "packfile-uris <comma-separated-list-of-protocols>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:376
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server that the client is willing to receive URIs of any of "
"the given protocols in place of objects in the sent packfile. Before "
"performing the connectivity check, the client should download from all given "
"URIs. Currently, the protocols supported are \"http\" and \"https\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:379
msgid ""
"If the 'wait-for-done' feature is advertised, the following argument can be "
"included in the client's request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:380
#, no-wrap
msgid "wait-for-done"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:384
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server that it should never send \"ready\", but should wait "
"for the client to say \"done\" before sending the packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:388
msgid ""
"The response of `fetch` is broken into a number of sections separated by "
"delimiter packets (0001), with each section beginning with its section "
"header. Most sections are sent only when the packfile is sent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:393
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    output = acknowledgements flush-pkt |\n"
"\t     [acknowledgments delim-pkt] [shallow-info delim-pkt]\n"
"\t     [wanted-refs delim-pkt] [packfile-uris delim-pkt]\n"
"\t     packfile flush-pkt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:400
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    acknowledgments = PKT-LINE(\"acknowledgments\" LF)\n"
"\t\t      (nak | *ack)\n"
"\t\t      (ready)\n"
"    ready = PKT-LINE(\"ready\" LF)\n"
"    nak = PKT-LINE(\"NAK\" LF)\n"
"    ack = PKT-LINE(\"ACK\" SP obj-id LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    shallow-info = PKT-LINE(\"shallow-info\" LF)\n"
"\t\t   *PKT-LINE((shallow | unshallow) LF)\n"
"    shallow = \"shallow\" SP obj-id\n"
"    unshallow = \"unshallow\" SP obj-id\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:409
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    wanted-refs = PKT-LINE(\"wanted-refs\" LF)\n"
"\t\t  *PKT-LINE(wanted-ref LF)\n"
"    wanted-ref = obj-id SP refname\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:412
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    packfile-uris = PKT-LINE(\"packfile-uris\" LF) *packfile-uri\n"
"    packfile-uri = PKT-LINE(40*(HEXDIGIT) SP *%x20-ff LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:415
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    packfile = PKT-LINE(\"packfile\" LF)\n"
"\t       *PKT-LINE(%x01-03 *%x00-ff)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:416
#, no-wrap
msgid "acknowledgments section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:421
msgid ""
"If the client determines that it is finished with negotiations by sending a "
"\"done\" line (thus requiring the server to send a packfile), the "
"acknowledgments sections MUST be omitted from the server's response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:423
msgid "Always begins with the section header \"acknowledgments\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:426
msgid ""
"The server will respond with \"NAK\" if none of the object ids sent as have "
"lines were common."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:429
msgid ""
"The server will respond with \"ACK obj-id\" for all of the object ids sent "
"as have lines which are common."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:432
msgid "A response cannot have both \"ACK\" lines as well as a \"NAK\" line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:437
msgid ""
"The server will respond with a \"ready\" line indicating that the server has "
"found an acceptable common base and is ready to make and send a packfile "
"(which will be found in the packfile section of the same response)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:444
msgid ""
"If the server has found a suitable cut point and has decided to send a "
"\"ready\" line, then the server can decide to (as an optimization) omit any "
"\"ACK\" lines it would have sent during its response.  This is because the "
"server will have already determined the objects it plans to send to the "
"client and no further negotiation is needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:445
#, no-wrap
msgid "shallow-info section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:453
msgid ""
"If the client has requested a shallow fetch/clone, a shallow client requests "
"a fetch or the server is shallow then the server's response may include a "
"shallow-info section.  The shallow-info section will be included if (due to "
"one of the above conditions) the server needs to inform the client of any "
"shallow boundaries or adjustments to the clients already existing shallow "
"boundaries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:455
msgid "Always begins with the section header \"shallow-info\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:458
msgid ""
"If a positive depth is requested, the server will compute the set of commits "
"which are no deeper than the desired depth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:461
msgid ""
"The server sends a \"shallow obj-id\" line for each commit whose parents "
"will not be sent in the following packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:466
msgid ""
"The server sends an \"unshallow obj-id\" line for each commit which the "
"client has indicated is shallow, but is no longer shallow as a result of the "
"fetch (due to its parents being sent in the following packfile)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:470
msgid ""
"The server MUST NOT send any \"unshallow\" lines for anything which the "
"client has not indicated was shallow as a part of its request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:471
#, no-wrap
msgid "wanted-refs section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:475
msgid ""
"This section is only included if the client has requested a ref using a "
"'want-ref' line and if a packfile section is also included in the response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:477
msgid "Always begins with the section header \"wanted-refs\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:480
msgid ""
"The server will send a ref listing (\"<oid> <refname>\") for each reference "
"requested using 'want-ref' lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:483
msgid ""
"The server MUST NOT send any refs which were not requested using 'want-ref' "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:484
#, no-wrap
msgid "packfile-uris section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:488
msgid ""
"This section is only included if the client sent 'packfile-uris' and the "
"server has at least one such URI to send."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:490
msgid "Always begins with the section header \"packfile-uris\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:493
msgid ""
"For each URI the server sends, it sends a hash of the pack's contents (as "
"output by git index-pack) followed by the URI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:497
msgid ""
"The hashes are 40 hex characters long. When Git upgrades to a new hash "
"algorithm, this might need to be updated. (It should match whatever "
"index-pack outputs after \"pack\\t\" or \"keep\\t\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:498
#, no-wrap
msgid "packfile section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:504
msgid ""
"This section is only included if the client has sent 'want' lines in its "
"request and either requested that no more negotiation be done by sending "
"'done' or if the server has decided it has found a sufficient cut point to "
"produce a packfile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:506
msgid "Always begins with the section header \"packfile\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:509
msgid "The transmission of the packfile begins immediately after the section header"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:516
msgid ""
"The data transfer of the packfile is always multiplexed, using the same "
"semantics of the 'side-band-64k' capability from protocol version 1.  This "
"means that each packet, during the packfile data stream, is made up of a "
"leading 4-byte pkt-line length (typical of the pkt-line format), followed by "
"a 1-byte stream code, followed by the actual data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:518
msgid "The stream code can be one of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:520
msgid "pack data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:521
msgid "progress messages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:522
msgid "fatal error message just before stream aborts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:524
#, no-wrap
msgid "server-option"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:530
msgid ""
"If advertised, indicates that any number of server specific options can be "
"included in a request.  This is done by sending each option as a "
"\"server-option=<option>\" capability line in the capability-list section of "
"a request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:532
msgid "The provided options must not contain a NUL or LF character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:534
#, no-wrap
msgid "object-format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:541
msgid ""
"The server can advertise the `object-format` capability with a value `X` (in "
"the form `object-format=X`) to notify the client that the server is able to "
"deal with objects using hash algorithm X.  If not specified, the server is "
"assumed to only handle SHA-1.  If the client would like to use a hash "
"algorithm other than SHA-1, it should specify its object-format string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:543
#, no-wrap
msgid "session-id=<session-id>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:548
msgid ""
"The server may advertise a session ID that can be used to identify this "
"process across multiple requests. The client may advertise its own session "
"ID back to the server as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:554
msgid ""
"Session IDs should be unique to a given process. They must fit within a "
"packet-line, and must not contain non-printable or whitespace "
"characters. The current implementation uses trace2 session IDs (see "
"link:technical/api-trace2.html[api-trace2] for details), but this may change "
"and users of the session ID should not rely on this fact."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:556
#, no-wrap
msgid "object-info"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:562
msgid ""
"`object-info` is the command to retrieve information about one or more "
"objects.  Its main purpose is to allow a client to make decisions based on "
"this information without having to fully fetch objects. Object size is the "
"only information that is currently supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:564
msgid "An `object-info` request takes the following arguments:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:565
#, no-wrap
msgid "size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:567
msgid "Requests size information to be returned for each listed object id."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:568
#, no-wrap
msgid "oid <oid>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:571
msgid ""
"Indicates to the server an object which the client wants to obtain "
"information for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:574
msgid ""
"The response of `object-info` is a list of the requested object ids and "
"associated requested information, each separated by a single space."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:576
#, no-wrap
msgid "\toutput = info flush-pkt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:579
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tinfo = PKT-LINE(attrs) LF)\n"
"\t\t*PKT-LINE(obj-info LF)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:581
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tattrs = attr | attrs SP attrs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:583
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tattr = \"size\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:585
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tobj-info = obj-id SP obj-size\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:587
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:591
msgid ""
"If the 'bundle-uri' capability is advertised, the server supports the "
"`bundle-uri' command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:597
msgid ""
"The capability is currently advertised with no value (i.e. not "
"\"bundle-uri=somevalue\"), a value may be added in the future for supporting "
"command-wide extensions. Clients MUST ignore any unknown capability values "
"and proceed with the 'bundle-uri` dialog they support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:601
msgid ""
"The 'bundle-uri' command is intended to be issued before `fetch` to get URIs "
"to bundle files (see linkgit:git-bundle[1]) to \"seed\" and inform the "
"subsequent `fetch` command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:606
msgid ""
"The client CAN issue `bundle-uri` before or after any other valid "
"command. To be useful to clients it's expected that it'll be issued after an "
"`ls-refs` and before `fetch`, but CAN be issued at any time in the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ^
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:608
#, no-wrap
msgid "DISCUSSION of bundle-uri"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:614
msgid ""
"The intent of the feature is optimize for server resource consumption in the "
"common case by changing the common case of fetching a very large PACK during "
"linkgit:git-clone[1] into a smaller incremental fetch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:617
msgid ""
"It also allows servers to achieve better caching in combination with an "
"`uploadpack.packObjectsHook` (see linkgit:git-config[1])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:622
msgid ""
"By having new clones or fetches be a more predictable and common negotiation "
"against the tips of recently produces *.bundle file(s).  Servers might even "
"pre-generate the results of such negotiations for the "
"`uploadpack.packObjectsHook` as new pushes come in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:627
msgid ""
"One way that servers could take advantage of these bundles is that the "
"server would anticipate that fresh clones will download a known bundle, "
"followed by catching up to the current state of the repository using ref "
"tips found in that bundle (or bundles)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ^
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:629
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROTOCOL for bundle-uri"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:634
msgid ""
"A `bundle-uri` request takes no arguments, and as noted above does not "
"currently advertise a capability value. Both may be added in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:643
msgid ""
"When the client issues a `command=bundle-uri` request, the response is a "
"list of key-value pairs provided as packet lines with value "
"`<key>=<value>`. Each `<key>` should be interpreted as a config key from the "
"`bundle.*` namespace to construct a list of bundles. These keys are grouped "
"by a `bundle.<id>.` subsection, where each key corresponding to a given "
"`<id>` contributes attributes to the bundle defined by that `<id>`.  See "
"linkgit:git-config[1] for the specific details of these keys and how the Git "
"client will interpret their values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:647
msgid ""
"Clients MUST parse the line according to the above format, lines that do not "
"conform to the format SHOULD be discarded. The user MAY be warned in such a "
"case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ^
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:649
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri CLIENT AND SERVER EXPECTATIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:651
#, no-wrap
msgid "URI CONTENTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:653
msgid "The content at the advertised URIs MUST be one of two types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:659
msgid ""
"The advertised URI may contain a bundle file that `git bundle verify` would "
"accept. I.e. they MUST contain one or more reference tips for use by the "
"client, MUST indicate prerequisites (in any) with standard \"-\" prefixes, "
"and MUST indicate their \"object-format\", if applicable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:664
msgid ""
"The advertised URI may alternatively contain a plaintext file that `git "
"config --list` would accept (with the `--file` option). The key-value pairs "
"in this list are in the `bundle.*` namespace (see linkgit:git-config[1])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:665
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri CLIENT ERROR RECOVERY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:670
msgid ""
"A client MUST above all gracefully degrade on errors, whether that error is "
"because of bad missing/data in the bundle URI(s), because that client is too "
"dumb to e.g. understand and fully parse out bundle headers and their "
"prerequisite relationships, or something else."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:677
msgid ""
"Server operators should feel confident in turning on \"bundle-uri\" and not "
"worry if e.g. their CDN goes down that clones or fetches will run into hard "
"failures. Even if the server bundle(s) are incomplete, or bad in some way "
"the client should still end up with a functioning repository, just as if it "
"had chosen not to use this protocol extension."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:680
msgid ""
"All subsequent discussion on client and server interaction MUST keep this in "
"mind."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:681
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri SERVER TO CLIENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:686
msgid ""
"The ordering of the returned bundle uris is not significant. Clients MUST "
"parse their headers to discover their contained OIDS and prerequisites. A "
"client MUST consider the content of the bundle(s)  themselves and their "
"header as the ultimate source of truth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:691
msgid ""
"A server MAY even return bundle(s) that don't have any direct relationship "
"to the repository being cloned (either through accident, or intentional "
"\"clever\" configuration), and expect a client to sort out what data they'd "
"like from the bundle(s), if any."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:692
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri CLIENT TO SERVER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:698
msgid ""
"The client SHOULD provide reference tips found in the bundle header(s)  as "
"'have' lines in any subsequent `fetch` request. A client MAY also ignore the "
"bundle(s) entirely if doing so is deemed worse for some reason, e.g. if the "
"bundles can't be downloaded, it doesn't like the tips it finds etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:699
#, no-wrap
msgid "WHEN ADVERTISED BUNDLE(S) REQUIRE NO FURTHER NEGOTIATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:705
msgid ""
"If after issuing `bundle-uri` and `ls-refs`, and getting the header(s)  of "
"the bundle(s) the client finds that the ref tips it wants can be retrieved "
"entirely from advertised bundle(s), the client MAY disconnect from the Git "
"server. The results of such a 'clone' or 'fetch' should be indistinguishable "
"from the state attained without using bundle-uri."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:706
#, no-wrap
msgid "EARLY CLIENT DISCONNECTIONS AND ERROR RECOVERY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:711
msgid ""
"A client MAY perform an early disconnect while still downloading the "
"bundle(s) (having streamed and parsed their headers). In such a case the "
"client MUST gracefully recover from any errors related to finishing the "
"download and validation of the bundle(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:714
msgid ""
"I.e. a client might need to re-connect and issue a 'fetch' command, and "
"possibly fall back to not making use of 'bundle-uri' at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:722
msgid ""
"This \"MAY\" behavior is specified as such (and not a \"SHOULD\") on the "
"assumption that a server advertising bundle uris is more likely than not to "
"be serving up a relatively large repository, and to be pointing to URIs that "
"have a good chance of being in working order. A client MAY e.g. look at the "
"payload size of the bundles as a heuristic to see if an early disconnect is "
"worth it, should falling back on a full \"fetch\" dialog be necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:723
#, no-wrap
msgid "WHEN ADVERTISED BUNDLE(S) REQUIRE FURTHER NEGOTIATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:727
msgid ""
"A client SHOULD commence a negotiation of a PACK from the server via the "
"\"fetch\" command using the OID tips found in advertised bundles, even if's "
"still in the process of downloading those bundle(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:735
msgid ""
"This allows for aggressive early disconnects from any interactive server "
"dialog. The client blindly trusts that the advertised OID tips are relevant, "
"and issues them as 'have' lines, it then requests any tips it would like "
"(usually from the \"ls-refs\" advertisement) via 'want' lines. The server "
"will then compute a (hopefully small) PACK with the expected difference "
"between the tips from the bundle(s) and the data requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:741
msgid ""
"The only connection the client then needs to keep active is to the "
"concurrently downloading static bundle(s), when those and the incremental "
"PACK are retrieved they should be inflated and validated. Any errors at this "
"point should be gracefully recovered from, see above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ^
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:743
#, no-wrap
msgid "bundle-uri PROTOCOL FEATURES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:750
msgid ""
"The client constructs a bundle list from the `<key>=<value>` pairs provided "
"by the server. These pairs are part of the `bundle.*` namespace as "
"documented in linkgit:git-config[1]. In this section, we discuss some of "
"these keys and describe the actions the client will do in response to this "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:754
msgid ""
"In particular, the `bundle.version` key specifies an integer value. The only "
"accepted value at the moment is `1`, but if the client sees an unexpected "
"value here then the client MUST ignore the bundle list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:759
msgid ""
"As long as `bundle.version` is understood, all other unknown keys MAY be "
"ignored by the client. The server will guarantee compatibility with older "
"clients, though newer clients may be better able to use the extra keys to "
"minimize downloads."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:764
msgid ""
"Any backwards-incompatible addition of pre-URI key-value will be guarded by "
"a new `bundle.version` value or values in 'bundle-uri' capability "
"advertisement itself, and/or by new future `bundle-uri` request arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:767
msgid ""
"Some example key-value pairs that are not currently implemented but could be "
"implemented in the future include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:770
msgid ""
"Add a \"hash=<val>\" or \"size=<bytes>\" advertise the expected hash or size "
"of the bundle file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:773
msgid ""
"Advertise that one or more bundle files are the same (to e.g. have clients "
"round-robin or otherwise choose one of N possible files)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:777
msgid ""
"A \"oid=<OID>\" shortcut and \"prerequisite=<OID>\" shortcut. For expressing "
"the common case of a bundle with one tip and no prerequisites, or one tip "
"and one prerequisite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:781
msgid ""
"This would allow for optimizing the common case of servers who'd like to "
"provide one \"big bundle\" containing only their \"main\" branch, and/or "
"incremental updates thereof."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/gitprotocol-v2.txt:786
msgid ""
"A client receiving such a response MAY assume that they can skip retrieving "
"the header from a bundle at the indicated URI, and thus save themselves and "
"the server(s) the request(s) needed to inspect the headers of that bundle or "
"bundles."
msgstr ""

